{"event_type":"review","id":"7a05b913ddf1698c75ec9c650ec4f157ec9fdb7a5fd6bbb1356d1485f693c5e3","occurred_at":"2026-11-05T15:19:24Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/849693f7cf00fca53bfce33abcdbc3585862fd535a237c69a929a35a714474d5","sha256":"849693f7cf00fca53bfce33abcdbc3585862fd535a237c69a929a35a714474d5"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/f3b6e1420fdbe31be575cf0ef729735231e156c74d4538bbfc367e9bb98b30f2","sha256":"f3b6e1420fdbe31be575cf0ef729735231e156c74d4538bbfc367e9bb98b30f2"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/24523729222d24a058403ee87d335521b917fa4b3b1a29a3b66a6ccb333f4ac5","sha256":"24523729222d24a058403ee87d335521b917fa4b3b1a29a3b66a6ccb333f4ac5"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/95688ac415c56ab7163b60b1dd6bb80108f43fa68e2646978c81c27b17a64bd4","sha256":"95688ac415c56ab7163b60b1dd6bb80108f43fa68e2646978c81c27b17a64bd4"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/96b03a5cfb9dd02b8c55d9f21cdf70d1a42031b4a29bc3f53a6045ec7fa441e9","sha256":"96b03a5cfb9dd02b8c55d9f21cdf70d1a42031b4a29bc3f53a6045ec7fa441e9"}],"attempt_id":"14664468765ee9ae8a1c6bf95844070de186a7564d2585256cca5b0a94f0bd66:0:1","base":"1059317cd58c5cd78d9d93687893cbd1f865c603","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"3fe39cba119a81e18e06d46f6c87fc67917c376c","body":"**Use links that work in the PR body.**\n\nGitHub copies this template into the PR description. The `../docs/...` links no longer have `.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md` as their base there, so they do not target the repository documents. Use GitHub's PR-body form, such as `../blob/main/docs/coderabbit-review.md`, for both references. ([docs.github.com](https://docs.github.com/en/communities/using-templates-to-encourage-useful-issues-and-pull-requests/about-issue-and-pull-request-templates?utm_source=openai))   \n\n\nAlso applies to: 50-50","id":"2a7a8bad28e65ee403eb89020b54b61cb3851112f0f36fab4c0522dcda1d3841","intervals":[],"path":".github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Use links that work in the PR body."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"426b15facb121254c6bc71b5e8f8ae04501a5816","body":"**Align `README.md:3` with the review policy.**\n\n`docs/coderabbit-review.md:5` says that no CLI cycle is required, and lines 7–10 define one independent exact-head review as the merge bar. The README currently makes the optional CLI cycle mandatory.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-Review protocol (one CodeRabbit CLI cycle before every PR, then one independent head-bound review): see [docs/coderabbit-review.md](docs/coderabbit-review.md).\n+Review protocol (one independent exact-head review): see [docs/coderabbit-review.md](docs/coderabbit-review.md).\n```\n\n</details>","id":"eaa7fb02ae569ac71007fa61dd8104617e63293f9730354e23ee3eda9757821e","intervals":[],"path":"README.md","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Align `README.md:3` with the review policy."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"52ae6eb9fe2ad06385bdb7aeb721b88ea168717a","body":"**Review lockfile-only dependency changes in CodeRabbit scope.**\n\nThe `!pnpm-lock.yaml` filter removes `pnpm-lock.yaml` from CodeRabbit's review. A PR that changes only resolved versions or integrity data in the lockfile gets no automated review of that diff. The CI steps that run `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` confirm that the lockfile matches `package.json`. They do not review the resolved changes. Remove the exclusion so that these changes receive review.\n\nDoctrine I2 covers acceptance by independent review of the head commit. It does not require CodeRabbit to review lockfile diffs, so this is a review-coverage gap rather than an I2 violation.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔧 Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-    - '!pnpm-lock.yaml'\n```\n\n</details>","id":"9ab4d557caf2db085c6038fa8ba24778177fc1ca2433d5d48ea98f5658858afa","intervals":[],"path":".coderabbit.yaml","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Review lockfile-only dependency changes in CodeRabbit scope."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"4c523a9da8bf14b18962271542707184f257e52c","body":"**Move `makeResolved` inside the per-attempt `try`.**\n\n`makeResolved` runs before the `try` that records attempt failures. If `createDriverFactory(...).resolve(...)` throws for a selected cell, `runCell` rejects. The top-level loop does not catch that rejection, so the script skips the remaining cells and does not emit Markdown or JSON output.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-      const resolved = await makeResolved(lane, provider, model, scratchDir);\n-      const driver = resolved.driver;\n       const startedAt = Date.now();\n       try {\n+        const resolved = await makeResolved(lane, provider, model, scratchDir);\n+        const driver = resolved.driver;\n```\n\n</details>","id":"6c610c6a5252991479570645d5bebdb30b4afe8fd26bc226dd0ad3630bceeaca","intervals":[],"path":"scripts/demo-eval-axes.mjs","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Move `makeResolved` inside the per-attempt `try`."}],"head":"fcf05bcbb2a5d0d1352fb3018e1358b673590696","head_tree":"013c2fa4bf520f2358e9d1367a3d73c21ab4fb44","input_scope":[{"blob":"52ae6eb9fe2ad06385bdb7aeb721b88ea168717a","intervals":[[1,209]],"path":".coderabbit.yaml"},{"blob":"3fe39cba119a81e18e06d46f6c87fc67917c376c","intervals":[[1,80]],"path":".github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md"},{"blob":"5a9be73609daa99678128e9bfc6c30ead155f4ec","intervals":[[1,382]],"path":".github/workflows/self-review-loop.yml"},{"blob":"426b15facb121254c6bc71b5e8f8ae04501a5816","intervals":[[1,282]],"path":"README.md"},{"blob":"4c523a9da8bf14b18962271542707